# g96-fu-connections: what the wiring applies (hot files; the rest of the task is committed)

## 1. compose_flip.rs: the connections composition call (around `compose_connections::compose_connections(`)

compose_connections no longer fails (a failed ssh folder preparation is reported at error level and leaves the core running), so
`.await?` becomes `.await`. ConnectionsInputs gains two fields:

  style: the ToastStyleReader the notify engine is built with (build it once above `NotificationEngine::new(..)`:
         `let toast_style: ToastStyleReader = { let config = config.clone(); Arc::new(move || ToastStyle::for_volume(config.desktop_settings().notification_volume)) };`
         pass `toast_style.clone()` to the engine and `style: toast_style` here),
  claims: `resource_claims.clone()`, an `Arc<crate::compose_connections::ResourceClaims>` made early (`let resource_claims: Arc<ResourceClaims> = Arc::default();`,
          before the server's claim hook is set).

## 2. host/claim: whoever records the claim sets the resources (mixdog-app-server outgoing.rs + server.rs, with the hook slot)

`ClaimHook::claimed` gets the claim's resources:

  fn claimed(&self, serves: &[HostCapability], resources: Option<&HostClaimResources>) -> Option<Box<dyn Any + Send>>;

`Outgoing::claim(host, conn, methods)` takes `resources: Option<HostClaimResources>` and passes `resources.as_ref()` to the hook;
server.rs `ClientRequest::HostClaim` passes `params.resources` (it already passes `params.serves`). `SystemProxyClaims::claimed` ignores the
new argument. The one hook slot then holds a hook that runs both (the claim keeps what each returns, dropped with the claim):

  pub struct ClaimHooks(pub Vec<Arc<dyn ClaimHook>>);
  impl ClaimHook for ClaimHooks {
      fn claimed(&self, serves: &[HostCapability], resources: Option<&HostClaimResources>) -> Option<Box<dyn Any + Send>> {
          let attached: Vec<Box<dyn Any + Send>> = self.0.iter().filter_map(|hook| hook.claimed(serves, resources)).collect();
          (!attached.is_empty()).then(|| Box::new(attached) as Box<dyn Any + Send>)
      }
  }

and the resources hook (compose_connections.rs is not a hot file but the trait is; this is the whole impl, put it beside ResourceClaims
once the trait has the new argument):

  impl ClaimHook for ResourceClaimHook(pub Arc<ResourceClaims>) { fn claimed(&self, _: &[HostCapability], resources: Option<&HostClaimResources>) -> Option<Box<dyn Any + Send>> { Some(self.0.attach(resources.cloned())) } }

(`ResourceClaims::attach(Option<HostClaimResources>)` is written and tested: it sets the resources and the returned guard clears them when the claim is
replaced or its connection closes; a newer claim attaches before the older is dropped and the older guard clears nothing.) Register
`ClaimHooks(vec![system_proxy_claims, Arc::new(ResourceClaimHook(resource_claims.clone()))])` where `set_claim_hook` is called today.

## 3. lib.rs: nothing new (compose_connections_language.rs is a #[path] submodule of compose_connections.rs).

## 4. SERVICE_PENDING: nothing to remove.
